      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 1892347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-03T09:39:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You don\u0027t *have* to disable the bitmap in this case. You can also just say that in edge-cases, it\u0027s okay for the bitmap to have a zero at an index where the node actually exists. (But we don\u0027t allow the bitmap to have ones when a node does not exist.)\n\nWith that approach, you handle failures to allocate by using `slow_desc_lookup` to find an unused id. You leave the bitmap unchanged.\n\nThe only other change you need is to `goto retry` instead of `BUG()` when the node already exists. That way, if the bitmap chooses an index for which a node already exists, then we update the bitmap with that information and try again with the next unused bit.",
      "revId": "aee6241db2502fdc29401c871476155b4cd683d2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "899302a2_63020b2c",
        "filename": "drivers/android/dbitmap.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
